<article class="env-definition" id="02Y1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02Y1">Definition <span data-tag="02Y1">4.39.3</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category. The <em>$2$-category of categories fibred in setoids over $\mathcal{C}$</em> is the sub $2$-category of the category of categories fibred in groupoids over $\mathcal{C}$ (see Definition <a href="/tag/02XS" data-tag="02XS">4.35.6</a>) defined as follows: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Its objects will be categories $p : \mathcal{S} \to \mathcal{C}$ fibred in setoids. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Its $1$-morphisms $(\mathcal{S}, p) \to (\mathcal{S}', p')$ will be functors $G : \mathcal{S} \to \mathcal{S}'$ such that $p' \circ G = p$ (since every morphism is strongly cartesian $G$ automatically preserves them). 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Its $2$-morphisms $t : G \to H$ for $G, H : (\mathcal{S}, p) \to (\mathcal{S}', p')$ will be morphisms of functors such that $p'(t_ x) = \text{id}_{p(x)}$ for all $x \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{S})$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>